cent"></span>Overview</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Why sleep pattern analysis matters</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><p>Sleep is where pain, anxiety and cognitive decline show themselves first. An arthritic dog does not limp at three in the morning, it repositions eleven times an hour, and no owner is awake to count that.</p><p>Sleep Pattern Analysis quantifies duration, fragmentation, position changes and circadian consistency, then flags deterioration in any of them.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Capabilities</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What this includes</h2></div><ul class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Fragmentation index</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">How often rest is interrupted, the clearest proxy for night-time discomfort.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Position change counting</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Repositioning frequency as an orthopaedic pain marker.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Circadian consistency</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Rhythm drift, a recognised early sign of canine cognitive dysfunction.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Environmental correlation</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Temperature, light and household noise matched against rest quality.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Recovery quality</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Whether rest after exertion is genuinely restorative.</p></div></li></ul></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center"><div><p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Outcomes</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What owners typically see</h2><ul class="mt-8 space-y-4"><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Osteoarthritis flagged from night-time restlessness before daytime lameness.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Objective measurement of whether pain relief is actually working.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Early identification of cognitive decline in senior animals.</li></ul></div><img alt="PawlogicTech hardware used for sleep pattern analysis" class="w-full rounded-3xl object-cover shadow-lift" decoding="async" height="900" loading="lazy" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_template_directory_uri() ); ?>/assets/images/tech-sensor.webp" width="1200"/></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>FAQ</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Sleep Pattern Analysis questions</h2></div><div class="divide-y divide-border rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card"><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">How much sleep is normal?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Adult dogs typically rest 12 to 14 hours a day, puppies and seniors considerably more, and cats 13 to 16 hours. The absolute figure matters far less than change against your own animal's established baseline.</p></details><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">My pet sleeps in my bed. Does that interfere?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">No. Movement signatures are separated by source, so your own movement does not contaminate your pet's record.</p></details></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 t